# React and UI conventions

React 19, TanStack Router, shadcn/ui (new-york style), Tailwind v4, lucide icons.

Visual layout and styling follow `design/` (see `design-folder` rule). Read mocks and
`design/assets/` before changing or adding components.

## Component shape

Named export, props as a named type, small private helpers above the exported
component in the same file.

```tsx
type PagePlaceholderProps = {
  title: string;
  note: string;
};

export function PagePlaceholder({ title, note }: PagePlaceholderProps) {
  return <div className="px-[22px]">{title}</div>;
}
```

## Imports

Use the `@/` alias for anything inside `packages/ui`, never deep relative paths.
Exception: a colocated test imports its subject as `./Component`.

```tsx
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";   // GOOD
import { Button } from "../../components/ui/button"; // BAD
```

## Styling

- Merge classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- Use theme tokens only: `bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-rule`,
  `bg-hair`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`. Never hardcode a hex or an
  arbitrary color. Brand values live in `@/lib/brand`.
- No `rounded-*` classes. Radius is `0` project-wide.
- Arbitrary pixel values matching the design are expected and fine:
  `h-[56px]`, `text-[12.5px]`, `gap-[18px]`.

## Files

- `components/ui/*` is generated by the shadcn CLI. Do not hand-edit; re-run the
  CLI to update.
- Prefer shadcn primitives (Select, Dialog, Toggle, fieldset) over reimplemented
  triggers and popover shells.
- Custom shared components go in `components/`, app chrome in `components/chrome/`.
- Route components go in `routes/`, named `<Name>Route.tsx`, and register in
  `router.tsx`.
- Hooks go in `hooks/`, named `use<Thing>.ts`, and throw if their context is missing.

## Accessibility

Every icon-only control needs an `aria-label`. Always set `type="button"` on
non-submitting buttons.

## Shortcut labels

Write shortcuts in plain words: `Press N`, `Cmd+K`, `Enter`, `Esc`, `Shift+N`.
Never use Mac glyph chips like `⌘N` or `↩`.
